Understanding the Role of a Physiotherapist
A physiotherapist is a healthcare professional trained to assess, diagnose, and manage physical impairments affecting movement and function.
The primary goal is not simply to relieve symptoms but to restore normal movement patterns and improve physical performance.
A qualified Physiotherapist in Mumbai typically begins treatment with a detailed assessment that includes:
Medical history review
Physical examination
Posture analysis
Joint mobility testing
Muscle strength evaluation
Functional movement assessment
Based on these findings, a customized treatment plan is developed.

Conditions Commonly Treated by Physiotherapists
Back Pain and Spine Disorders
Back pain remains one of the leading reasons patients seek physiotherapy.
Common conditions include:
Lumbar strain
Herniated disc
Sciatica
Postural back pain
Degenerative spine conditions
Targeted exercises, manual therapy, and posture correction help reduce discomfort while improving spinal stability.
Neck Pain and Cervical Problems
Long hours spent on computers and mobile devices have increased neck-related complaints throughout Mumbai.
Physiotherapy can help manage:
